{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","text":"Importing at call sites","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but that re-exports ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}]},{"text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"store.killswitch.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The easy case to forget is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that reads the slice for display — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to that file.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison","type":"heading","level":3},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action knowledge"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"None","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","type":"heading","level":2},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"yes"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","text":"Hook Selection Guide","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush() async"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registration-Order","text":"Registration Order","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}]},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","title":"Design Principles","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","title":"PluginHost","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","kind":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","kind":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"title":"EntityStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"}}}